#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1453 expect=noViolation domain=DI
#note "DISEQ restarts per SPDEVID: DEV-1 has DISEQ 1,2 and DEV-2 has DISEQ 1,2 -> the same sequence numbers on different devices are fine because SPDEVID is part of the key (DOMAIN, SPDEVID). No class= on the dataset line — the twin declares none. ADAPTED-FROM fda/FDA-SD1453/FDA-SD1453-valid-DI.cdt (verbatim)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DI
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SPDEVID  type=Char label="Sponsor Device Identifier"
col DISEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DIPARMCD type=Char label="Device Identifier Element Code"
col DIPARM   type=Char label="Device Identifier Element Name"
col DIVAL    type=Char label="Device Identifier Element Value"
---
S1 | DI | DEV-1 | 1 | DEVTYPE | Device Type   | PUMP
S1 | DI | DEV-1 | 2 | MANUF   | Manufacturer  | ACME
S1 | DI | DEV-2 | 1 | DEVTYPE | Device Type   | SENSOR
S1 | DI | DEV-2 | 2 | MANUF   | Manufacturer  | ACME
